Day 04 – Problems on Numbers

Topic:
• Problems on Numbers
• Sum of Two Numbers
• Sum of Squares
• Finding Product of Two Numbers

What I Learned:
• How to find the product when the sum of two numbers and sum of their squares are given
• Used the identity (x + y)² = x² + y² + 2xy
• Learned to identify the given values and apply the formula

Formula:
• Product = [(Sum)² − Sum of Squares] / 2

Example:
If the sum of two numbers is 27 and the sum of their squares is 509:

Product = (27² − 509) / 2
        = (729 − 509) / 2
        = 220 / 2
        = 110

Answer: 110

Key Learning:
First identify the sum and sum of squares, then apply the formula to find the product.
